  "hypothesis": {
    "mechanism": "Keep the full control pass unchanged. Use only already-accepted pre-fusion person candidates from the unchanged full-frame plus 640px-tile control to identify at most one crowd/overlap cluster. Run exactly one additional 512px source-space crop for that cluster, using the unchanged model/input size/confidence/decoder settings and no enhancement. Admit only person detections centered inside the bounded trigger region, then use the existing hard-NMS final merge.",
    "non_goals": [
      "No generic confidence-threshold search",
      "No global 512px tiling",
      "No enhancement or low-light preprocessing",
      "No revival of evidence-aware, conservative-NMM, weighted fusion, or other previously rejected fusion policies",
      "No production/control behavior change before later blinded gates"
    ],
    "summary": "A single evidence-triggered 512px microtile around one crowded/overlapping baseline person cluster can recover some small or occluded low-contrast pedestrians without the global duplicate/false-positive pressure caused by replacing all 640px tiles with 512px tiles."
  },
