  "predicted_failure_modes": [
    "Crowd or clutter clusters may trigger an extra crop without containing a missed pedestrian, increasing false positives.",
    "The microtile may split one real person into multiple boxes whose overlap is below hard-NMS suppression, increasing duplicate pressure.",
    "Isolated low-contrast misses with no neighboring accepted baseline person evidence are intentionally not addressed.",
    "A 512px crop can remove useful context for large or edge-of-frame people.",
    "Crowd-heavy clips may activate the one-call budget on many frames, increasing compute even if quality does not improve."
